			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b6f072d9-85d7-444d-954a-5f466b322350")
	)
	(text "Firmware toggles WDI in software (50-1000 Hz, ~50% duty) only while the control loop is healthy.\nNever drive WDI from a timer/PWM: a timer keeps running after the CPU hangs.\nEach falling edge on WDI pulls the Q7001 gate low through C7001 and tops up C7002 via R7003.\nWD_OK ~2.7 V while toggling. WDI stuck high, low or floating: <1 V in ~100 ms, <0.4 V in ~190 ms\n(10 uF nominal; DC-bias derating shortens this). WD_OK starts at 0 V at power-up (fail-safe).\nWD_OK drives N-FET gates only (14.4 V rail switch, water pump, LiDAR incl. laser): no resistive loads.\nWDI pin: high-Z at reset, no pull-down. All parts reuse existing BOM lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 259.08 320.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d4676a50-1e11-4bb3-b61e-385409f401e5")
	)
